## Execution Plan
Follow this plan step by step:
1. In `src/interface/content/contentCard.ts`, define and export the `ContentCard` interface with fields: `uid: string`, `title: string`, `description?: string`, `url?: string`, `image?: string`, and a `__metadata?: Record<string, unknown>` field for Contentstack editable metadata.

2. In `src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx`, create and export `ContentstackProvider` that initializes Contentstack Live Preview via `ContentstackLivePreview.init({ stackSdk: window.contentstack, enable: true })`, stores `livePreviewData` and `isPreviewEnabled` in React state, subscribes to `window.contentstack` events to update state on entry changes, and provides values through a `ContentstackContext` with type `{ livePreviewData: Record<string, unknown> | null; isPreviewEnabled: boolean; setLivePreviewData: (data: Record<string, unknown>) => void }`.

3. In `src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx`, also export a `useContentstackContext()` hook that calls `useContext(ContentstackContext)` and throws a descriptive error if used outside `ContentstackProvider`.

4. In `src/hooks/useContent.ts`, export a `useContent<T extends ContentCard>(entry: T): { content: T; isPreviewEnabled: boolean }` hook that reads `livePreviewData` from `ContentstackContext`, merges any preview overrides into the passed `entry`, and returns the merged content along with `isPreviewEnabled`.

5. In `src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLink/ContentstackLink.tsx`, export a `ContentstackLink` component with signature `(props: { href: string; children: React.ReactNode; metadata?: Record<string, unknown> }) => JSX.Element` that renders an `<a>` tag and, when `metadata` is present, spreads Contentstack editable attributes (`data-cs-editable`, `data-cs-metadata`) onto the anchor element.

6. In `src/components/contentstack/ContentstackImage/ContentstackImage.tsx`, export a `ContentstackImage` component with signature `(props: { src: string; alt: string; metadata?: Record<string, unknown> }) => JSX.Element` that renders an `<img>` tag and, when `metadata` is present, applies Contentstack editable attributes (`data-cs-editable`, `data-cs-metadata`) to the image element.

7. Write unit tests for `ContentstackProvider` verifying that it provides default context values, that `useContentstackContext` throws when called outside the provider, and that `setLivePreviewData` updates context state.

8. Write unit tests for `useContent` verifying that it returns the original entry when no preview data exists and returns merged data when `livePreviewData` contains matching fields.

9. Write unit tests for `ContentstackLink` and `ContentstackImage` verifying that editable attributes are applied when `metadata` is provided and omitted when it is not.
